  "body": "### Signing update - 2026-09-09\n\nWindows executables were re-signed without rebuilding: **Fara Technologies LLC**\nis the primary signer and **Mike Fara** is the second signer. Both signatures\nuse SHA256 and RFC3161 timestamps. EXEs inside ZIP/MSIX downloads use this order;\nMSIX container publisher identities are unchanged. Existing checksum files\nwere refreshed. Linux/macOS assets and Store-unsigned submissions are unchanged.\n\nFresh GitHub **verification attestations** cover the current replacement Windows\ndownloads and updated checksum files. The [verification workflow](https://github.com/faratech/htop-win/actions/runs/34372906452)\nchecked their SHA256 hashes against the reviewed manifest and validated the Windows\nsignatures, including EXEs inside archives. No signing credentials were used.\n\nVerify a downloaded asset (replace `FILE` with its filename):\n\n```sh\ngh attestation verify FILE --repo faratech/htop-win --predicate-type https://faratech.dev/attestations/windows-release-verification/v1 --signer-workflow faratech/htop-win/.github/workflows/attest-existing-release.yml\n```\n\nThese attestations cover **hash and signature verification, not compilation or\nsource-to-binary provenance**. The original build attestations still describe the\noriginal hashes. Use the explicit predicate type above; the default command expects\nbuild provenance. Checksum files are hash-checked only. You can also check embedded\nsignatures with `signtool verify /pa /all <file.exe>` (extract ZIPs first).\n\n---\n\nhtop-win v0.2.9\n\nFixes unstable selection and screen jumping when sorting by changing process metrics (#86). Normal viewing preserves the selected row; explicit follow mode tracks process identity.\n\n- Capture immutable process targets when opening kill confirmations, including tagged batches (#87).\n- Validate parent process identity before tree navigation and branch actions (#88).\n- Preserve visible process rows on many-core systems and selection visibility after resizing (#10, #90).\n- Fix installed-version detection, VIRT accounting, and metadata retry caching (#91, #92, #72).\n- Correct executable-path and unsupported environment-inspection labels (#93).\n- Keep error diagnostics visible and scrollable; render and truncate emoji as complete graphemes (#94, #15).\n- Repair release workflow YAML and add workflow linting (#89).\n\nValidation: 158 Windows tests pass, all-target Clippy passes with warnings denied, workflow validation passes, and x64/ARM64 release builds launch successfully.\n\n### Verification\n\nBoth binaries are signed with Azure Trusted Signing. Verify their Authenticode signatures with:\n\n```bash\nsigntool verify /pa /all htop-win-amd64.exe\nsigntool verify /pa /all htop-win-arm64.exe\n```\n"
